course: dictionary
lesson: 28
title: Holding back: the word abstemious
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Abstemious is a formal word. It means eating and drinking very little, especially not much rich food or alcohol. A person who is abstemious holds back from pleasures on purpose.
explain: Look for clues in the words around it. «She chose an abstemious life, with simple meals and no sweets.» Simple meals and no sweets show that she eats very little and holds back, so abstemious must mean careful and sparing with food and drink.
explain: Abstemious is close in meaning to moderate, which means not too much. It is not the same as sad or lazy. It is a choice to hold back, like the self-control shown in «abstemious habits».
fact: Abstemious means eating and drinking very little.
fact: «An abstemious life» is a life with little rich food, few treats and not much alcohol.
fact: Abstemious is a formal word, so you will meet it in books and history more than in everyday talk.
fact: In church life, fasting in Lent is an abstemious practice, because people give up some foods and pleasures for a time.
fact: The word «abstemious» contains the vowels a, e, i, o, u in that order, just like «facetious».
exercise: «She lived an abstemious life, with simple meals and no treats.» What does abstemious mean? | Singing loudly all day | Living in a big house | *Eating and drinking very little | Eating a huge feast every night
exercise: Ben says abstemious means greedy. What does it really mean? | *Holding back, eating and drinking very little | Very greedy for rich food | Loud and cheerful | Happy and lively
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to abstemious? | Lazy | *Moderate | Greedy | Noisy
test: Monks in old stories often lived abstemious lives. What does this tell you about them? | Monks ate huge feasts every day | Monks were always singing loudly | *Monks ate and drank very little and held back from pleasures | Monks liked sweets best of all
test: In «abstemious habits», what do the habits show about a person? | Love of loud music | Wild, careless fun | Fear of the dark | *Self-control and holding back from pleasures
exam: Which sentence uses abstemious correctly? | The abstemious guest spent all his money on rich food and sweets | *The abstemious guest took one small slice of cake and only a sip of juice | The abstemious guest was shouting and dancing all night | The abstemious guest ate a huge feast and asked for seconds and dessert
